sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant PER001 as PER-001 Customer
    participant APP as SVC-017 Digital Channels
    participant SVC013 as SVC-013 Fraud Detection
    participant EVTBUS as SVC-102 Event Bus
    participant SVC001 as SVC-001 Retail Banking Core
    participant SVC053 as SVC-053 Notification Service
    participant SVC111 as SVC-111 WORM Store
    participant PER054 as PER-054 Fraud Analyst
    participant PER059 as PER-059 Senior Manager

    Note over PER001,PER059: PH-064 — Fraud Alert Trigger

    PER001->>APP: Report fraud via mobile app
    APP->>SVC013: POST /fraud-cases (trigger_type=customer_report)
    SVC013->>SVC013: Create FraudCase status=open. Publish FraudCaseCreated (EVT-090)
    SVC013-)SVC053: Dispatch case confirmation to PER-001

    Note over PER001,PER059: PH-065 — Case Creation

    PER054->>SVC013: GET /fraud-cases/{id}
    Note over SVC013,EVTBUS: Cross-capability async: CAP-004 → CAP-001 via Event Bus (no direct sync calls)
    SVC013-)EVTBUS: Publish FraudDataRequested (payment_intent_id)
    EVTBUS-)SVC001: SVC-001 consumes FraudDataRequested — retrieves PaymentIntent
    SVC001-)EVTBUS: Publish FraudDataProvided (£28,000, cop_result=no_match, cop_override_confirmed=true, fraud_risk_level=high)
    EVTBUS-)SVC013: SVC-013 consumes FraudDataProvided
    PER054->>SVC013: POST /fraud-cases/{id}/evidence (evidence_type=cop_result, psr_relevance=supports_gross_negligence)
    PER054->>SVC013: PATCH /fraud-cases/{id} status=investigating. Publish FraudInvestigationStarted (EVT-091)

    Note over PER001,PER059: PH-066 — Investigation

    SVC013-)EVTBUS: Publish FraudWarningLogRequested (payment_intent_id) [cross-capability async: CAP-004→CAP-001]
    EVTBUS-)SVC001: SVC-001 consumes FraudWarningLogRequested — retrieves payment_warning_log
    SVC001-)EVTBUS: Publish FraudWarningLogProvided: CoP no_match acknowledged 14:23:05Z + fraud warning 'Continue anyway' 14:23:07Z + high-risk confirmation 14:23:12Z
    EVTBUS-)SVC013: SVC-013 consumes FraudWarningLogProvided
    PER054->>SVC013: POST /fraud-cases/{id}/evidence (evidence_type=payment_warning_log, psr_relevance=supports_gross_negligence)
    PER054->>SVC013: PATCH /fraud-cases/{id} vulnerability_assessment=[none_identified]
    PER054->>SVC013: POST /fraud-cases/{id}/evidence (evidence_type=communication_log — contradictory customer statements)
    PER054->>SVC013: PATCH /fraud-cases/{id} status=decision_pending

    Note over PER001,PER059: Analyst identifies gross negligence + value > £25,000 — mandatory escalation to PER-059

    PER054->>PER059: Escalate: decline decision + value £28,000 require Senior Manager co-sign

    Note over PER001,PER059: PH-067 — Reimbursement Decision (Senior Manager review)

    PER059->>SVC013: GET /fraud-cases/{id} — review case and all evidence
    SVC013-->>PER059: Full FraudCase + FraudEvidence (CoP log, warning acknowledgements, vulnerability assessment)
    PER059->>SVC013: PATCH /fraud-cases/{id} (senior_manager_sign_off=true, senior_manager_id={manager_id})
    PER054->>SVC013: POST /fraud-cases/{id}/decision (decision=decline, gross_negligence_evidence='...', senior_manager_sign_off=true)
    SVC013->>SVC013: Validate senior_manager_sign_off=true. Update FraudCase status=declined. Publish FraudReimbursementDeclined (EVT-093)
    SVC013-)SVC053: Dispatch regulated outcome letter (decline) — plain language, FOS signpost mandatory
    SVC053-)PER001: Email: Outcome letter — not eligible for reimbursement. Right to complain to FOS within 6 months.

    Note over PER001,PER059: No ReimbursementCredited. No ReimbursementClaim. SVC-001 and SVC-009 take no payment action on EVT-093.

    SVC001-)SVC001: Consume EVT-093 — no credit action (optional: customer account monitoring flag)

    Note over PER001,PER059: PH-070 — Case Closure

    PER054->>SVC013: PATCH /fraud-cases/{id} status=closed
    SVC013->>SVC013: Set closed_at. Publish FraudCaseClosed (EVT-097). Publish FraudPatternDetected (EVT-098). PSR quarterly counter: declined case.
    SVC013-)SVC111: Archive full case (including gross_negligence_evidence) to WORM — 7yr retention for FOS evidence
